  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MHPSS Somalia 2024 &#x2013; WHO MHPSS Technical Working Group Coordinator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia is currently facing a complex and protracted humanitarian crisis driven by ongoing conflict, terrorism, civil unrest, and recurring climatic shocks. Decades of conflict, frequent outbreaks of cholera and measles, pervasive poverty, and recurring climatic shocks&#x2014;including the recent drought and subsequent floods&#x2014;have severely undermined Somalia&#x2019;s already fragile health system. As a result of these compounded challenges, a significant portion of the population, particularly the youth, is grappling with deep-seated psychological issues that have largely gone unaddressed.Recent data from the Federal Ministry of Health (FMOH) and the World Health Organization (WHO) (2023) indicate a high prevalence of mental disorders, with anxiety disorders being the most common. Conflict and insecurity affect men and women differently, with women and children often being the most vulnerable and hardest hit. Women, in particular, are more susceptible to abuses and various forms of gender-based violence (GBV), including rape, sexual assault, forced prostitution, and domestic violence.In 2018, over 76 percent of recorded GBV survivors were from internally displaced persons (IDP) communities. Additionally, widespread practices such as Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) and early forced marriage pose significant risk factors for mental illness and psychosocial disruption among women. To this end, the technical working group (TWG) requires an experienced MHPSS specialist to support the TWG coordination to ensure coordination in Mogadishu, Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
